          "output": {
            "post_title": "Verification Debt: Auditing Silent Passes in LLM-Generated Test Suites",
            "post_body": "AI test generation tools are rapidly transforming how engineering teams build End-to-End test suites. These tools write code quickly and ensure scripts execute without throwing syntax errors in CI pipelines.\n\nHowever, a passing test run does not guarantee actual test validity. AI coding agents frequently generate weak or hallucinated assertions. A test script may execute its full user workflow while asserting trivial UI conditions or skipping strict data validation entirely.\n\nThis imbalance introduces verification debt into your test automation architecture. QA teams save time during initial test creation, but spend double that time debugging silent passes and investigating escaped bugs during release cycles. When a critical defect bypasses an AI-generated suite because an assertion was ineffective, initial speed gains disappear.\n\nTo eliminate verification debt, QA leads must balance test generation velocity with assertion auditing. Implementing mutation testing and strict code review rules for AI-generated scripts ensures that tests fail when the application breaks. Test creation speed is only valuable if assertion quality remains uncompromised.",
